course: dictionary
lesson: 7061
title: Patchy and uneven
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Patchy means it appears in some places but not in others. Think of a patchwork quilt: some bits are one colour and some bits are another, so the whole thing is not the same everywhere. «Patchy rain» means some areas get rain and others stay dry.
explain: Patchy can also describe work or knowledge. «Patchy work» in a school report means some of it is good and some of it is poor. The words around the word give the clue: is it describing places, like fog, or results, like work?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The phone signal was patchy on the bus» means the signal came and went in different places. If you put in "even" and the sentence still works, you may have the right idea.
fact: Patchy means appearing in some places but not others, or not good everywhere.
fact: «Patchy fog» means fog in some areas and clear air in others.
fact: «Patchy knowledge» means you know some parts well and other parts not so well.
fact: «One coat of paint often looks patchy, so a second coat is painted on once the first is dry.»
fact: Patchy is an adjective, and its comparing forms are patchier and patchiest.
exercise: «The weather forecast says there will be patchy rain.» What does patchy rain mean? | There will be no rain at all | Rain falls everywhere, all day and all night | *Rain falls in some areas and not in others | Rain falls only on the hills
exercise: Mrs Patel writes, «Ravi's work this term is patchy.» What does she mean? | His work is perfect in every part | His work is finished early every week | He has not done any work at all | *His work is good in some parts and weak in others
exercise: Mia's phone signal kept dropping on the bus. Which word fits best? | ancient | glum | curt | *patchy
test: «The fog was patchy, so we could see the church in some places but not others.» What does patchy mean here? | Gone for ever | *In some places but not others | Very thick and grey everywhere | Soft and fluffy
test: Oliver says his science report is patchy. What does he mean? | *Some parts are good and some parts are poor | It is written in a different language | It is perfect all the way through | It is very long
exam: Why is a second coat of paint often painted on? | To make the room smaller | *To cover the patchy bits so the paint looks even | To make the first coat wetter | To stop the paint from drying
